On **.NET 10 SDK**, you **no longer need `TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport`**. That property was the .NET 9 (and earlier) bridge. Instead, add a `"test"` section to your `global.json`:

```json
{
  "sdk": {
    "version": "10.0.100"
  },
  "test": {
    "runner": "Microsoft.Testing.Platform"
  }
}
```

This tells `dotnet test` to use MTP natively — arguments pass through directly (no `--` separator needed).

You can then **remove** `<TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>true</TestingPlatformDotnetTestSupport>` from your `.csproj`.

